      "text": "lest there be an uproar among the people, Matt. 26:5. Pilate saw … a tumult was made, Matt. 27:24. wasted his substance with riotous living, Luke 15:13. hearts be overcharged with surfeiting, Luke 21:34. Jews which believed not … set all the city on an uproar, Acts 17:5. called in question for this day’s uproar, Acts 19:40. after the uproar was ceased, Paul called, Acts 20:1. Jerusalem was in an uproar, Acts 21:31. Let us walk honestly … not in rioting, Rom. 13:13. in imprisonments, in tumults, 2 Cor. 6:5. lest there be … tumults, 2 Cor. 12:20. revellings … they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom, Gal. 5:21. faithful children not accused of riot or unruly, Titus 1:6. wrought the will of the Gentiles, when we walked in … revellings, 1 Pet. 4:3. run not with them to the same excess of riot, 1 Pet. 4:4. count it pleasure to riot in the day time, 2 Pet. 2:13.",
